rtw88: support a second AP on 8822B

The firmware beacon engine repeats exactly one reserved page, while mac80211
hands out a beacon per BSS on demand.  Allow two AP interfaces on 8822B and
give the second one its own beacons:

 - register the interface combination for 8822B and raise the AP limit to 2;
 - pin the firmware page to a stable vif pointer instead of a port number,
   because mac80211 recycles ports when an interface is restarted;
 - make ap_active a refcount and keep BIT_EN_BCNQ_DL, the DTIM register and
   the page ownership in line with the number of running APs;
 - drive the beacons of the AP that does not own the page from an hrtimer
   and send them through the mgmt ring, since the beacon queue only feeds
   the auto-repeating page.

Downstream only: it builds on the beacon/rsvd-page rework and the AP
channel-switch series, none of which is upstream.

